  "premise": "A word with {name}, who walks with the player between scenes: small talk, their view of things, and, slowly, who they are. It has nothing to settle and moves nothing in the story on (the next place waits on the map); it lasts until the player says goodbye or walks on.",
  "truth": "Nothing in a talk is hidden from the GM but what {name} keeps back of their own story: their lore and memories say who they are and how things stand between them and the player, and each talk's prep fills in the one thing they might confide this time (the discovery), if there's one. A talk moves nothing in the story on.",
