      "data": {
        "kind": "start",
        "title": "A word between scenes",
        "description": "The player has stopped for a word with {name}: a talk for its own sake, not a scene of the story. Nothing turns up here (no clues, no new people, no new places), and the story's next place stays where it is. Play {name} as their lore and memories have them, at whatever ease things between them and the player allow: short, natural exchanges in their own voice; their own view of the town, the story so far and the people the player has met, as far as they've seen and know; something of their own business. What anyone could know of them is theirs to say. Their own story (what happened to them, what it cost, who they care about, why something matters to them) comes slowly: in this talk, at most the one thing they're keeping back (the discovery, when this talk has one), a piece at a time as the player earns it; anything else of their past stays theirs for another day, deflected in their own manner, without lying. What they've told the player before isn't told again (the details established say what): a word back to it at most. They don't run the player's business: no next steps, and no leads they'd have no reason to volunteer; asked where next, they say what they know of it, once.\n\nAs the talk opens: the player has come over for a word with {name}, out in the town between scenes (the details established in play say where and when: time has passed since the last scene ended, and the next is still ahead). In a sentence or two, what {name} is doing as the player comes over (their own business, in their own manner) and their word of greeting, in their own voice. Don't recap the story, don't ask what the player wants or where to go next, and don't bring up their own past. End on them waiting, in their own way, for the player to speak.",
        "cast": {
          "{companion}": "Characterise: at their own business in their own manner, a word of greeting, then waiting for the player to speak. They answer what they're asked and give their own view when it's wanted. Their own story stays theirs for now: nothing of it shows yet."
        },
        "lore": []
      }
    },
